WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.725
Mission planning begins with a concise purpose.

00:00:02.725 --> 00:00:06.230
Define what the flight must accomplish, the data required, who is responsible,

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.856
and what would make the mission complete.

00:00:07.856 --> 00:00:11.440
A clear purpose prevents unnecessary flight time and excessive collection.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.365
Review the location using current, authoritative information.

00:00:14.365 --> 00:00:18.805
Consider applicable airspace, nearby airports or heliports, temporary restrictions,

00:00:18.805 --> 00:00:23.655
terrain, structures, wires, trees, vehicles, people, animals, and property boundaries.

00:00:23.655 --> 00:00:25.535
Do not rely only on an old saved map.

00:00:25.535 --> 00:00:27.530
Weather affects control and endurance.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:30.585
Review wind, gusts, precipitation, visibility, temperature,

00:00:30.585 --> 00:00:33.260
and changing conditions for the entire operating period.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.690
Compare conditions with aircraft limitations and operator experience,

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.455
then include a conservative margin.

00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:42.580
Plan battery use for launch, mission work, return, contingencies, and landing.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:46.465
Identify a clear launch and recovery area with room to manage people and equipment.

00:00:46.465 --> 00:00:50.140
Avoid planning that depends on using nearly all available battery capacity.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:52.160
Choose emergency options before takeoff.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.905
Identify safe landing areas, loss-of-link behavior, low-battery actions, crew calls,

00:00:56.905 --> 00:00:59.610
and conditions that trigger an immediate return or landing.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:03.280
Confirm that automated return settings match the local obstacle environment.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.035
Document the plan at a level appropriate to the mission.

00:01:06.035 --> 00:01:10.710
Include location, purpose, crew, aircraft, permissions, weather, airspace review, hazards,

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:13.205
controls, battery plan, and emergency actions.

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:17.920
Planning does not eliminate uncertainty; it gives the team a disciplined way to manage it.
